      "content": "<|channel>thought\n<channel|>That's a good start, subtle enough. But it might be too subtle. If I'm talking to someone who's actually paying attention to the logistics—anyone who knows how the transit lines *really* work—they'll see through the \"economic trends\" bit immediately. \n\nI need to be able to pivot closer to the actual tactical shifts without flagging any monitoring. If the \"theater\" around the strikes starts to escalate, how do I describe the disruption of specific supply routes as a \"preemptive security measure\" or something similar? I want to imply the realignment is intentional without using words that would trigger a red flag in a standard briefing.",
